        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "17d6136c-3801-5c45-9157-5375192d456f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1994–95 FA Cup, 2008 FA Cup victory\n- People: Joe Royle, Harry Redknapp\n- Organizations: Everton, Portsmouth, Central Coast Mariners, Wimborne Town, Southern Football League\n- Concepts: World War II suspension, English-born managers\n\nFacts:\n- The 1994–95 FA Cup was the 50th FA Cup officially held since the six-year suspension caused by World War II.\n- Everton manager Joe Royle won the 1994–95 FA Cup and was the last English-born manager to lift the trophy until Harry Redknapp led Portsmouth to the 2008 FA Cup victory.\n- Harry Redknapp is an advisor to Central Coast Mariners.\n- Harry Redknapp is a director at Wimborne Town, a club in the Southern Football League.",
